## Plan

_Written by `claude-3` (claude, `sonnet`, medium) ([run](https://github.com/Jlore-Studios/JackiOh/actions/runs/42089855645)) before anyone built this. The night bot's builder starts from this section: edit it here to change the plan._

## Goal

Add `apps/web/src/spacing.css`, a named spacing scale that `index.css` imports beside the other scales. Move every `gap`, `padding` and `margin` in the board sheets onto it, with each value rounded to a step by at most 2 px. Add `src/spacing.test.ts`, which holds the board sheets to zero fixed lengths and every other sheet to its allowlisted count, which can only go down. Describe the scale in `apps/web/README.md`. CSS and web tests only: no spec section, ruling or crate applies.

## Files to touch

| File | | What |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/spacing.css` | new | `:root` with `--space-1` to `--space-11` |
| `apps/web/src/spacing.test.ts` | new | the scale, the board rule and the `UNMIGRATED` allowlist |
| `apps/web/src/index.css` | change | import `spacing.css` after `motion.css`; migrate its spacing; `--gap` |
| `apps/web/src/game/{activate,animations,board,clock,facedown,lanePick,leanNewest,market,modifierList,notices,overflow,prompt,reveal,starscape,trade}.css` | change | migrate spacing; `board.css` also has two `--gap` lines |
| `apps/web/src/game/{craft/craft,drag/drag,showcase/showcase}.css` | change | migrate spacing |
| `apps/web/README.md` | change | one paragraph after the motion paragraph (line 54) |
| `apps/web/src/routes/Rematch.test.tsx` | change | line ~234 asserts `padding: 8px 18px` in `animations.css` |
| `apps/web/src/cards/cardState.test.tsx` | change | line ~504 asserts `padding:\s*0 3px` on `board.css`'s `.board button.buried-badge` |

Do not touch these: `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/`, `.claude/`, `crates/`, `spec/`, `game/deckbuilder/*`, `game/table.css`, and any menu sheet (`routes/`, `auth/`, `practice/` and the rest). Those keep their raw lengths, and the allowlist freezes them.

## Decisions

The issue's example is a pure 4 px scale. I chose a scale that is 2 px-granular up to 12 px, because the board's most used lengths are 6 px (about 100 uses) and 10 px (about 60). On a 4 px scale each of those moves by 2 px. Re-pick this if you prefer the example.

- **Steps.** 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40 px, numbered `--space-1` to `--space-11`.
- **Rounding.** Round to the nearest step, counting `0` as a step. A tie goes to the smaller one. Nothing grows by more than 2 px (the largest are 30→32 and 14.4→16), and a menu page can't newly overflow spec 46.
- **Composed lengths.** 28, 36, 48 and 132 px are 4 px or more from any step, so they are composed from steps and stay exact.
- **Relative terms stay.** `em`, `%`, `vh` and `env()` terms and `var(--tray-channel)` stay. An `em` spacing scales with its box, as the type scale's em forms do.
- **Rem.** `rem` becomes px at 16 px, because `html` sets no size. Those rems are all in `game/market.css`.
- **`--gap`.** `--gap` was `6px`, and `4px` on a phone. It becomes `var(--space-3)`, and `var(--space-2)` on a phone.

## Steps

1. Create `apps/web/src/spacing.css`:
```css
/* The client's one spacing scale (#3225): every board stylesheet's gap, padding and margin names a step
   here, or is 0, auto, an em or % term, an env() or a viewport or container term (src/spacing.test.ts).
   A step is a length in px, smallest first, numbered from 1: 2px apart to 12px, where the board's own
   lengths sit, then 4px and 8px apart. A new step goes in order and raises the list in that test. */

:root {
  --space-1: 2px;
  --space-2: 4px;
  --space-3: 6px;
  --space-4: 8px;
  --space-5: 10px;
  --space-6: 12px;
  --space-7: 16px;
  --space-8: 20px;
  --space-9: 24px;
  --space-10: 32px;
  --space-11: 40px;
}
```
2. In `apps/web/src/index.css`, add `@import "./spacing.css";` on its own line right after `@import "./motion.css";`. The existing import-order regexes in `typescale.test.ts`, `surfaces.test.ts` and `motion.test.ts` anchor only on a prefix, so they still pass.
3. Save the script below as `/tmp/migrate-spacing.mjs`, outside the worktree, and run `node /tmp/migrate-spacing.mjs apps/web/src` from the repo root. Expect "rewrote 482 values; 4 left for hand" and four `MANUAL` lines.
```js
import { readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync, writeFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { join, relative } from "node:path";
const SRC = process.argv[2];
const sheets = (dir) => readdirSync(dir).flatMap((n) => { const p = join(dir, n); return statSync(p).isDirectory() ? (n === "test" ? [] : sheets(p)) : n.endsWith(".css") ? [p] : []; });
const BOARD = sheets(SRC).map((p) => relative(SRC, p).replaceAll("\\", "/"))
  .filter((s) => s === "index.css" || (s.startsWith("game/") && !s.startsWith("game/deckbuilder/") && s !== "game/table.css"));
const STEPS = [2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40];
const MANUAL = new Set([28, 36, 48, 132]);
const PROP = /(?<![\w-])((?:grid-)?(?:row-|column-)?gap|padding(?:-(?:top|right|bottom|left|inline|block)(?:-(?:start|end))?)?|margin(?:-(?:top|right|bottom|left|inline|block)(?:-(?:start|end))?)?|--gap)(\s*:\s*)([^;}]+)/g;
const RAW = /(?<![\w.])(-?)(\d*\.?\d+)(px|rem)\b/g;
const nearest = (px) => { let best = 0; for (const s of STEPS) if (Math.abs(s - px) < Math.abs(best - px)) best = s; return best; };
let changed = 0, manual = 0;
for (const sheet of BOARD) {
  const path = join(SRC, sheet);
  const text = readFileSync(path, "utf8");
  const out = text.split(/(\/\*[\s\S]*?\*\/)/).map((part, i) => i % 2 === 1 ? part : part.replace(PROP, (_all, prop, colon, value) => {
    if (prop === "--gap") return prop + colon + value.replace(/^6px$/, "var(--space-3)").replace(/^4px$/, "var(--space-2)");
    return prop + colon + value.replace(RAW, (tok, sign, num, unit) => {
      const px = Number(num) * (unit === "rem" ? 16 : 1);
      if (px === 0) return tok;
      if (MANUAL.has(px)) { manual++; console.log(`MANUAL ${sheet}: ${prop}: ${value.trim()}`); return tok; }
      const best = nearest(px); changed++;
      if (best === 0) return "0";
      const step = `var(--space-${STEPS.indexOf(best) + 1})`;
      return sign === "-" ? `calc(${step} * -1)` : step;
    });
  })).join("");
  if (out !== text) writeFileSync(path, out);
}
console.log(`rewrote ${changed} values; ${manual} left for hand`);
```
The results are `1px`→`0`, `-4px`→`calc(var(--space-2) * -1)`, `max(6px, env(…))`→`max(var(--space-3), env(…))`. Spot-check these:

| px | step | px | step | px | step | rem | becomes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2, 3 | 1 | 10, 11 | 5 | 20, 22 | 8 | 0.25, 0.3 | 2 |
| 4, 5 | 2 | 12, 14 | 6 | 24 | 9 | 0.4 | 3 |
| 6, 7 | 3 | 16, 18 | 7 | 30 | 10 | 0.5 / 0.75 | 4 / 6 |
| 8, 9 | 4 | | | | | 0.9, 1 / 1.25 / 1.5 | 7 / 8 / 9 |

4. Hand-edit the four `MANUAL` spots (find each by its content):
   - `game/animations.css` (about line 1698): `padding: var(--space-8) 28px var(--space-8);` becomes `padding: var(--space-8) calc(var(--space-9) + var(--space-2)) var(--space-8);`.
   - `index.css` `.app-shell` (about line 226): the final `48px` becomes `calc(var(--space-10) + var(--space-7))`.
   - `index.css` under `@media (max-width: 560px)` (about line 645): the final `36px` becomes `calc(var(--space-10) + var(--space-2))`.
   - `game/prompt.css` (about line 869): `padding-bottom: calc(env(safe-area-inset-bottom) + 132px);` becomes `…+ var(--space-11) * 3 + var(--space-6));`.
5. Verify with `grep -n -- "--gap:" apps/web/src/index.css apps/web/src/game/board.css`. Expect `var(--space-3)` in `index.css` and `var(--space-2)` twice in `board.css`.
6. Update the two unit tests that read board CSS text (see Tests). Neither imports the CSS, so the harness's `--changed` run would skip them. Run them yourself.
7. Create `apps/web/src/spacing.test.ts` (see Tests).
8. In `apps/web/README.md`, insert this paragraph after the motion paragraph, with a blank line between: "The spacing is one scale (#3225): `src/spacing.css`, imported by `index.css` after the motion, names eleven lengths, `--space-1` (2px) to `--space-11` (40px): 2px apart to 12px, where the board's own lengths sit, then 16, 20, 24, 32 and 40px. A board stylesheet gives every `gap`, `padding` and `margin` (and the `--gap` they read) a step, `0`, `auto`, or a `calc()`, `clamp()` or `max()` holding one, and may keep an `em` or `%` term (it scales with its box), a viewport or container term and `env()`, never a px or rem length of its own. A length that is no step is composed of steps (`calc(var(--space-9) + var(--space-2))`), and a negative one is a step times -1. `src/spacing.test.ts` checks this and holds every other stylesheet to its count of px and rem lengths in `UNMIGRATED`; a sheet that loses some lowers its number."

## Tests

`apps/web/src/spacing.test.ts` is written in the manner of `typescale.test.ts`. Copy its `SRC`, `files()`, `SHEETS`, `read` and `BOARD_SHEETS` (the same filter, "as palette.test.ts has them"), and add `codeOf = (sheet) => read(sheet).replace(/\/\*[\s\S]*?\*\//g, " ")`. Then add exactly:

```ts
const SPACING = /(?<![\w-])((?:grid-)?(?:row-|column-)?gap|padding(?:-(?:top|right|bottom|left|inline|block)(?:-(?:start|end))?)?|margin(?:-(?:top|right|bottom|left|inline|block)(?:-(?:start|end))?)?|--gap)\s*:\s*([^;}]+)/g;
const FIXED = /(?<![\w.])(\d*\.?\d+)(?:px|rem)\b/g;

function rawSpacing(css: string): string[] {
  const code = css.replace(/\/\*[\s\S]*?\*\//g, " ");
  const found: string[] = [];
  for (const match of code.matchAll(SPACING)) {
    const value = (match[2] ?? "").trim().replace(/\s+/g, " ");
    for (const length of value.matchAll(FIXED)) if (Number(length[1]) !== 0) found.push(`${match[1] ?? ""}: ${length[0]} (${value})`);
  }
  return found;
}
const STEPS = [...read("spacing.css").matchAll(/^\s*--space-(\d+):\s*(\d+)px;$/gm)].map((match) => ({ name: Number(match[1]), px: Number(match[2]) }));
```

`const UNMIGRATED: Record<string, number>` holds the table below. It is what the test computes on the untouched sheets, 62 sheets and 1599 lengths in all. If a count differs for a sheet you did not edit, your regex has a typo. Fix the regex, not the number.

```
