cards/cards.css 10; cards/inspect/inspect.css 95; cards/inspect/list-play.css 4; cards/keywords.css 5; cards/marks.css 2;
cards/tallies.css 3; cards/wheel/wheel.css 13; collection/collection.css 44; collection/tokenOffer.css 5; dungeon/dungeon.css 14;
dungeon/fight/fight.css 11; dungeon/map/run.css 37; dungeon/stats/dungeon-stats.css 23; duos/duos.css 60; economy/economy.css 21;
economy/jlore-pill.css 4; economy/xp.css 7; emotes/emotes.css 32; emotes/portrait.css 10; empty/empty.css 4;
game/deckbuilder/deckbuilder.css 88; game/deckbuilder/workshop.css 89; i18n/language.css 4; notfound/notfound.css 3;
packs/pack-object.css 2; packs/packs.css 11; patches/patches.css 98; practice/practice.css 145; practice/sandbox.css 13;
rank/rankCrest.css 2; rank/streakFlame.css 1; replay/replay.css 2; routes/account.css 11; routes/command-menu.css 11;
routes/dev-panel.css 7; routes/entry-card.css 9; routes/game-banner.css 9; routes/landing.css 54; routes/leaderboard.css 3;
routes/lobby.css 129; routes/privacy.css 4; routes/purchases.css 2; routes/replays.css 5; routes/site-footer.css 5;
routes/stats.css 85; routes/top-bar.css 1; settings/changeEmail.css 4; settings/settings.css 43; shop/shop.css 17;
shortcuts/kbd.css 1; sideline/sideline.css 7; skeleton/skeleton.css 5; together/together.css 53; tutorial/path-visibility.css 12;
tutorial/tutorial.css 115; undo/undo.css 3
```
Write it as `"audio/audio.css": 12,` one per line.

The five tests, in `describe("#3225 the spacing scale")` and `describe("#3225 no one-off spacing")`:

1. `it("#3225 spacing.css names eleven lengths in px, smallest first, as --space-1 up, and nothing else")`:
   - `STEPS.map(px)` equals `[2,4,6,8,10,12,16,20,24,32,40]`.
   - `STEPS.map(name)` equals `STEPS.map((_, i) => i + 1)`.
   - The comment-stripped file, with the `--space-N: Npx;` lines removed and whitespace removed, is `":root{}"`.
   - `index.css` matches `/^@import "\.\/fonts\.css";\n@import "\.\/palette\.css";\n@import "\.\/typescale\.css";\n@import "\.\/surfaces\.css";\n@import "\.\/motion\.css";\n@import "\.\/spacing\.css";\n/`.
2. `it("#3225 every var(--space-…) names a step, and only spacing.css declares one")`. For each sheet, every `/var\((--space-[\w-]+)\)/g` match in `codeOf` is in the set of `--space-<name>`. Any sheet but `spacing.css` has no `/--space-[\w-]+\s*:/`.
3. `it("#3225 the checker counts a px or rem length in a gap, padding or margin, and nothing else")`. Run `rawSpacing` on this CSS:
   ```
   a { padding: 6px var(--space-2) 0 0.2em 4%; margin: -4px 0 0 -4px; gap: calc(var(--space-2) * -1) 1.5rem; --gap: 4px; }
   b { padding: max(0px, env(safe-area-inset-top)) 3vh; margin-inline: auto; gap: var(--gap); width: 9px; padding-bottom: calc(env(x) + 12px) }
   ```
   Map each entry to `entry.split(" (")[0]`. Expect `["padding: 6px","margin: 4px","margin: 4px","gap: 1.5rem","--gap: 4px","padding-bottom: 12px"]`.
4. `it("#3225 the board's stylesheets give every gap, padding and margin a step, zero, auto, or a relative or env() term")`. `BOARD_SHEETS.length > 20`, and the flat list of `${sheet}: ${entry}` from `rawSpacing(read(sheet))` equals `[]`.
5. `it("#3225 no other stylesheet gains a fixed spacing of its own")`. For every sheet except `spacing.css` and the board sheets, count `rawSpacing(read(sheet)).length`. The sheets with a count above 0 form a record that equals `UNMIGRATED`.

Edit the two existing tests:
- `routes/Rematch.test.tsx`: in the regex at line ~234 replace `padding: 8px 18px;` with `padding: var\(--space-4\) var\(--space-7\);`.
- `cards/cardState.test.tsx`: replace `/padding:\s*0 3px/` with `/padding:\s*0 var\(--space-1\)/`.

Commands, from the repo root:
- `sh scripts/build-wasm.sh`
- `pnpm --dir apps/web exec vitest run src/spacing.test.ts src/typescale.test.ts src/surfaces.test.ts src/motion.test.ts src/palette.test.ts src/routes/Rematch.test.tsx src/cards/cardState.test.tsx`
- `pnpm --dir apps/web test`, the whole unit suite once, because many tests read CSS text
- `pnpm --dir apps/web typecheck`
- `pnpm exec eslint apps/web/src/spacing.test.ts`
- `cargo jackioh classify --base origin/main --claims`

For e2e, run `pnpm --dir e2e exec cypress verify` first. If it succeeds, run `pnpm --dir e2e test:component`, then specs `46` and `47` as `e2e/README.md` describes. If Cypress is missing, say "not run" in the report. Do not call it green. CI's e2e smoke runs 46 and 47 per pull request. I found no golden image under `e2e/`, since the component specs measure boxes, so none gets updated.

## Done when

- [ ] `spacing.css` exists and `index.css` imports it after `motion.css`.
- [ ] The README paragraph is in.
- [ ] Every board sheet's gap, padding, margin and `--gap` is on the scale, and the four composed lengths are hand-edited.
- [ ] The `spacing.test.ts` tests pass, as do `typescale`, `surfaces`, `motion` and `palette`, the two edited tests and the full web suite.
- [ ] Typecheck and eslint are clean.
- [ ] The harness's rustfmt, catalog, patches, rulings, clippy, cargo-test and web-test checks are green. A web-only change leaves the Rust ones untouched.
- [ ] No file outside the table is changed (`git status`), and `git diff -- game/deckbuilder game/table.css` is empty.
- [ ] The final report lists the e2e specs run, or says plainly that Cypress could not run.
- [ ] The report records the decisions above.

## Risks

- **Layout shift.** Every rounding is at most 2 px. All but two shrink or stay: 30→32 in `board.css`' `.board[data-log="open"] > .log`, and 0.9rem→16 in `game/market.css`. The 6 px shell padding that `mobile-ux.cy.tsx` pins (378 and 832 px) is exact.
- **Hairline spacing.** A shrinking 1 px to `0` in tags and pills (14 values) is the likeliest visible change. A `margin: -1px` in the visually hidden turn-banner and `.showcase-live` becomes `0`, which is harmless for a clipped absolute 1×1 box.
- **Specs not run here.** I could not run the Cypress component specs and 46/47 in planning. CI's smoke run will catch a break in 46 or 47.
- **Fixed-unit tests.** Other tests may pin board CSS text I did not find. I searched for `padding|margin|gap` assertions and found two; the full web suite run is the net.
- **Idempotence.** Re-running the script is harmless (no raw lengths left except the four manual ones).

## Open questions

- Should the scale be the issue's pure 4 px example? That would move every 6 px and 10 px by 2 px. I kept 6 and 10 as steps.
- Is keeping `em` and `%` terms as "relative terms" in the board sheets acceptable? The issue's list names only viewport and container terms. Converting em to px would break scaling in the badges that use it (`handHints`, `prompt`, `showcase`, `spent`).
- The rem to px conversion makes `game/market.css` ignore a raised browser font size.

The item stays `difficulty:medium`: it is client CSS and tests, about 25 files, with no engine, AI, migration or cross-crate design.
